<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Höfe District</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Höfe is a district of the Swiss canton of Schwyz on the southern shore of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-zurich">Lake Zurich</a>, made up of the municipalities of Wollerau, Freienbach and Feusisberg. It belonged to the abbey of Einsiedeln and to Zürich, which ceded it to Schwyz in 1440 after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-zurich-war">Old Zürich War</a>. The acquisition gave Schwyz a foothold on Lake Zurich and its trade route.</p></div>
